course: dictionary
lesson: 8634
title: Scurry: quick, small steps
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To scurry means to run or move quickly with short, fast steps, like a mouse. You can also scurry when you are in a rush or a bit afraid. Look for the clue: «the Rabbit drops the gloves and fan and scurries away into the darkness» tells you the Rabbit is in a hurry to get away.
explain: Scurry is a vivid verb. A writer can choose it instead of "run" to paint a picture for the reader. Think of mice, crabs, beetles and squirrels: all of them scurry.
explain: Try swapping your meaning into a sentence. In «a whole hidden town scurries away», the creatures are small and quick, so scurries fits. Does your meaning still make sense?
explain: Scurry can also be a noun. A scurry is a hurried movement or the sound of one, as in a scurry of feet.
fact: Scurry means to move quickly with short, fast steps, or to hurry because you are in a rush or afraid.
fact: «Lift a log or a stone and a whole hidden town scurries away»: the creatures are woodlice, centipedes, millipedes and beetles.
fact: The text tells us woodlice are cousins of crabs.
fact: Useful phrases: scurry away, scurry about, scurry off, a scurry of feet.
fact: As a noun, scurry means a hurried movement or the sound of it.
exercise: «When Alice timidly says "If you please, sir—", the Rabbit drops the gloves and fan and scurries away into the darkness.» What does scurries mean here? | Sits down slowly to rest | *Moves away quickly in a hurry | Shouts loudly at Alice | Falls asleep in the dark
exercise: Which of these creatures might scurry? | A cloud | *A mouse | A cup of tea | A tall tree
exercise: In the phrase "a scurry of feet", what is a scurry? | *A hurried movement or the sound of it | A loud song | A kind of shoe | A slow, quiet walk
test: Which word best replaces "ran" in "The mouse ___ across the kitchen floor"? | *scurried | ate | slept | smiled
test: In the phrase "scurry off", what does off show? | The creature is asleep | *The hurrying creature leaves | The creature is hungry | The creature arrives
exam: Why is "scurry" a better choice than "run" in "The crabs ___ over the rocks when the waves came in"? | It is a longer word | *It paints a quick, busy picture of small creatures hurrying | It shows the crabs are happy and slow | It means to sleep under the rocks
